      {
        "kind": "ai",
        "text": "Karajishi, “Chinese lions”, were guardian beasts Japan knew only from Chinese and Buddhist art; no one painting them had seen a lion. Huge and striding across gold, they are an emblem of power fit for a warlord's hall."
